  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Innovation Resource Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Innovation Resource Facility (IRF) is a rapid procurement mechanism designed to provide the Australian Aid with efficient access to additional technical advisory services in development innovation as well as enhance DFAT and AGO innovation capabilities beyond aid. The IRF will also implement the Australian Development Accelerator pilot to provide seed finance metors risk cover and tehnical support to development innovations sourced by Australian posts and divisions. 
The IRF seeks to provide the Australian Aid program and its partners access to additional technical advisory services in frontier fields of development including innovative finance products (eg crowd-sourced equity, outcome-based aid), innovative development techniques (eg human-centred and problem driven design techniques), and new development technologies (eg GIS mapping, mobile surveys, other digital technologies to improve poor peoples access to front line services).  The IRF will also administer the Development In</narrative>
  </description>
